  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the **exact solutions in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=-\\sqrt{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies outside the given domain its not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=2\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$",
